IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Advance Australia Logo Protection Act 1984 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND
-- THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A02884.txt
-- (compilation No. 2, 10 December 2015). The trader using the logo asks: "Did
-- I infringe the monopoly in the logo's design; does it infringe the copyright;
-- can I be sued for use before the Act?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 11(1)(a)-(d).
DECLARE `Dealing` IS ONE OF
    `applying the design to an article`
    `selling or hiring an article to which the design was applied in infringement`
    `importing for sale or trade an article to which the design was applied outside Australia`
    `selling or hiring an imported article bearing the design`

DECLARE `Logo case` HAS
    `my dealing`                                                IS A `Dealing`
    -- s 11(1): "the design or any fraudulent or obvious imitation of it"
    `the design or a fraudulent or obvious imitation is involved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have the owner's licence`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day I do it`                                           IS A DATE
    -- s 15(2)
    `I acted under a purported licence`                         IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Logo position` HAS
    `I infringe the monopoly in the design`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the prescribed period ended on`                            IS A DATE
    `I infringe the copyright in the logo`                      IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `no action lies against me`                                 IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 3(1): "the period of 16 years that commenced on 13 October 1983".
@ref s 3(1) prescribed period
`the start of the prescribed period` MEANS Date 13 10 1983
`the end of the prescribed period` MEANS Date 12 10 1999

GIVEN c IS A `Logo case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is within the prescribed period` c IF
        c's `the day I do it` AT LEAST `the start of the prescribed period`
    AND c's `the day I do it` AT MOST `the end of the prescribed period`

-- s 11(1): (a) and (b) only "without the licence of the owner"; (c) and (d)
-- carry no such words and are read as written (F1).
@ref s 11(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Logo case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I infringe the monopoly` c IF
        `it is within the prescribed period` c
    AND c's `the design or a fraudulent or obvious imitation is involved`
    AND (   NOT (c's `I have the owner's licence`)
         OR c's `my dealing` EQUALS `importing for sale or trade an article to which the design was applied outside Australia`
         OR c's `my dealing` EQUALS `selling or hiring an imported article bearing the design`)

-- s 19(2)-(3): during and after the prescribed period, an act the design's
-- owner has (or would have had) the exclusive right to do does not infringe
-- the copyright. Before it, the Copyright Act alone answers: NOTHING.
@ref s 19(2)-(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Logo case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`do I infringe the copyright` c MEANS
    IF c's `the day I do it` AT LEAST `the start of the prescribed period`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 15(2): no action for use before 13 October 1983 in accordance with a
-- purported licence.
@ref s 15(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Logo case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no action lies` c IF
        c's `the day I do it` LESS THAN `the start of the prescribed period`
    AND c's `I acted under a purported licence`

@ref ss 3, 11, 15, 19
@export default The position of a trader dealing with articles bearing the Advance Australia logo under the Advance Australia Logo Protection Act 1984 (Cth): whether they infringed the monopoly in the design (s 11: applying the design or an imitation without licence, selling or hiring infringing articles, or importing or dealing in articles bearing it, during the 16 years from 13 October 1983 to 12 October 1999); that their dealing does not infringe the copyright in the logo from 13 October 1983 (s 19(2)-(3)); and whether no action lies for use before 13 October 1983 under a purported licence (s 15(2)). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Logo case`  @desc My dealing, whether the design or an imitation is involved, any licence, and the day
GIVETH A `Logo position`
`the logo position for` c MEANS
    `Logo position` OF `I infringe the monopoly` c, `the end of the prescribed period`, `do I infringe the copyright` c, `no action lies` c
